{
  "Year": 1969,
  "Level": "AMC 12",
  "Batch": "NA",
  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 29,
  "Question": "If \\(x=t^{\\frac{1}{t-1}}\\) and \\(y=t^{\\frac{t}{t-1}},\\) \\(t\\gt0,\\) \\(t\\ne1,\\) a relation between \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(y^x=x^{\\frac{1}{y}}\\)",
    "B": "\\(y^{\\frac{1}{x}}=x^y\\)",
    "C": "\\(y^x=x^y\\)",
    "D": "\\(x^x=y^y\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Comparing the given exponents helps express \\(y\\) in terms of \\(x\\). Because \\(t>0\\) and \\(t\\ne1\\), all the exponents are defined and both \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are positive. Thus positive-base real-power laws apply:\n\\[\ny=t^{t/(t-1)}\n=\\left(t^{1/(t-1)}\\right)^t=x^t.\n\\]\nDividing the original expressions also gives\n\\[\n\\frac{y}{x}\n=t^{\\frac{t}{t-1}-\\frac{1}{t-1}}\n=t^{\\frac{t-1}{t-1}}=t,\n\\]\nso \\(y=tx\\). Combining these two relationships,\n\\[\ny^x=(x^t)^x=x^{tx}=x^y.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(\\boxed{y^x=x^y}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\), holds throughout the stated domain.",
